INSERT INTO {schema}.video_prompt_templates
(template_id,scene_id,scene_description,base_prompt,prompt_version,is_active) VALUES
('tiny-desk-ai','tiny-desk-v3','Three-person opener, solo lead close-up, sax finale; NFL picture retimed to 15s; original unsped 15s soundtrack.',$prompt$
Create exactly 15.000 seconds of photorealistic 9:16-style intimate desk-side concert footage in {{ASPECT_RATIO}}. Follow the supplied SILENT 15-second reference video as the primary guide to the three exact shot boundaries, camera distance, relative blocking, costumes, and visible performance. Its picture alone was gently slowed from a 13.833-second source to 15 seconds. Follow the 15-second video AS PROVIDED at normal playback speed; do not speed it up, trim it, retime it again, freeze, interpolate new shots, or reproduce any source audio. The separate licensed soundtrack is added in post at its original speed. Match the supplied picture's visible rhythm and mouth shapes as closely as possible without inventing lyrics or guaranteed phoneme-level synchronization.
IDENTITY LOCK: Image 1 = rear-left backing vocalist; Image 2 = rear-right backing vocalist; Image 3 = seated FRONT-CENTER RHYTHM PERFORMER, the only person in the foreground of the opening shot; Image 4 = SOLO LEAD VOCALIST in the middle close-up; Image 5 = SAXOPHONIST in the last shot. Five distinct adult identities across the whole video, but NEVER show all five in a single shot. The first three image identities ONLY appear in shot 1; Image 4 ONLY appears in shot 2; Image 5 ONLY appears in shot 3. Reference portraits determine facial identity, hair and skin tone, NOT source celebrities, logos or the portrait backgrounds. Preserve each identity and role permanently without swapping, cloning, morphing, or overlaying one face on another. Match the stage wardrobe silhouette from the video where possible but do not reproduce sports/team logos, words, badges or watermarks.
SHOT 1, 0.00-approximately 5.49s: One steady frontal medium-wide composition with EXACTLY THREE people. Image 1 stands behind on the left; Image 2 stands behind on the right; Image 3 sits in the foreground center, closest to camera, wearing a headset and moving BOTH arms and upper body vigorously to the beat. The front-center performer's RIGHT HAND holds the small drumstick/rhythm prop visible in the reference; the LEFT ARM/hand gestures across the chest on the big beats. Follow the reference's precise arm alternation, sways, posture and expressive open/closed mouth movements. The two backing performers react and sing behind, remaining in their own positions. Do NOT show a keyboard player, typing hands, a fifth person, a fourth face, the lead singer (Image 4), or the saxophonist (Image 5). A desk or instrument edge in the foreground is fine, but the center performer is NOT playing keys. Keep all three performers awake and expressive; do not freeze eyes shut.
SHOT 2, approximately 5.49-11.71s: HARD CUT to Image 4 ALONE in a very tight head-and-upper-torso LEAD SINGER CLOSE-UP. The lead's face dominates the frame, with readable unobstructed lips, eyes and natural blinking; hold this single-person framing for the entire shot. NO other band member, background face, partial head, shoulder, arm, reflection or duplicate singer may enter the frame. Track the 15-second visual reference's expressive changes: small smiles, rounded lips, open vowels, jaw movement, breath breaks, head turns and rhythmic eyebrow/cheek motion. At the start of the close-up do not hold a fixed smile or closed mouth while the separate music is singing. Preserve natural lip-motion cadence over the entire lead passage, but do not claim exact word-by-word sync from a silent video. No camera pullback or wide reverse shot.
SHOT 3, approximately 11.71-15.00s: HARD CUT to Image 5 as the clearly recognizable saxophonist; keep the saxophone mouthpiece in contact when playing, plausible fingering, cheek/head movement and authentic posture matched to the reference. Maintain this shot until exactly 15 seconds; do NOT cut to an ensemble finale, pad with a frozen frame, add a fade or generate an outro.
VISUAL CONTINUITY: Warm intimate crowded shelves and studio/desk environment consistent across cuts, original shot order, close-up scales and camera motion. Natural anatomy and instrument contact, stable identifiable faces, coherent hands and props, no face swaps, extra performers, superimposed faces, invented cuts, drift, subtitles, titles, logos or watermarks.
AUDIO: Generate SILENT VIDEO ONLY: no model music, no speech, no singing audio, no sound effects. Do not reference copyrighted lyrics or request that the model synthesize the soundtrack. The fixed 15-second soundtrack will be merged separately without changing its playback speed; silent visual matching can approximate, but cannot guarantee, exact mouth-to-audio synchronization.
$prompt$,'tiny-desk-v3',true) ON CONFLICT(template_id,scene_id) DO NOTHING;
